 you don't have a lot of time  to get a lot of stuff done so you have  to be super productive in that time that  you do spend so my email is an hour and  a half of that and if i don't answer  everybody within that hour and a half  then it goes to the next day's email so  i find that to be super helpful for me I  used to be an email freak and answering  all the time and I found that it  prevented me from be able to do some  real work so typically how my week will  work right now I guess on Monday again  I'll get in the office of one and I'll  usually check email and then in the  afternoon I'll have two chunks of time  so you know just say chunk and chunk  what I'll do here is a task for the week  so this could be writing a no blog post  doing my facebook stuff for the week  i'll try to schedule as much stuff as  possible in advance so like facebook  posts i might plan out the entire week  on monday so that it's all ready set to  go my youtube videos i'll have already  them they'll be all edited and then I'll  on Monday I'll set them up for the whole  week to go out so as much as possible if  you find yourself doing repetitive tasks  you either want to chunk them up  together so you're more productive doing  those tasks you do them all at once and  then schedule them out or also look for  ways to automate things delegate things  or maybe even eliminate things so as  I've grown my business we brought on a  team of people who helped me with a  whole bunch of different things in my  business so this could be different task  and then I also leave some time for what  I call CEO time and these are important  tasks that I used to grow my business  that is not working on my business in my  business but more working on my business  so it could be hiring new staff working  on a new project testing out something  new that I want to work on for the  website or my business things that are  will grow the business that are kind of  admin keep me tied into the kind of day  to day with my company so that's monday  monday is always a super busy day I  don't schedule any calls or anything  else on Monday because I'm so busy  creating everything that  to do basically for the entire week  anything that has to get done for the  week basically gets done on monday and  then i'm done so that's Monday on  Tuesday I'll also get in at one o'clock  and I'll check my email and then that's  it for the day the rest of the day I  still have my two other chunks and both  of these are just CEO times and this  just gives me a chance to work on big  projects that sometimes take a lot of  time so if I'm writing you know a book  for example or creating new content that  I want to expand my business so i need  to do interviews something that is  really going to help grow my business  that'll be here so i found that having  an entire day to be able to focus on  that really helps so i'll be done my  email at two-thirty and then have a hat  15 minute break and then to forty five  to six o'clock with a little break in  between the basin working on all CEO  business growth stuff and you'll find  that your growth can really take off the  more you're working on your business  versus in so setting up system setting  up processes hiring new people other  plans that i have to grow my business  testing things out that's all part of my  CEO time so tuesdays are a lot of fun  I've gotten all my work for the week out  of the way on monday and i still have my  email to the handle on tuesday i still  check the once a day but then i have the  rest of it to be able to do stuff to  grow my business wednesday is a touch  different wednesday i'll usually get in  at 10 and i'll start doing my videos so  these videos it's a wednesday morning  i'm doing the videos i used to do them  at one o'clock but i found that the  light wasn't enough coming and i got big  windows here at my office but I get more  morning sunshine than afternoon sunshine  so I found the video quality was better  when I was filming in the morning so  I'll come in and start doing my videos  right away and then  after I'll take a break so do that do a  break and I'll go with my wife and we  usually go to Starbucks and chapters the  chapters is a bookstore here so like  barnes and nobles and we'll just relax  and plan our lives when my son is at  school might read things that we want to  read or talk about what we want to work  on it's just kind of relaxed time for  the two of us and then I'll get back in  the afternoon afternoon and here all you  should do more videos but these will be  the tutorial type so sometimes people  ask me to do videos and I'll explain it  using my computer instead of be actually  on camera or I'll walk through tutorials  of how I use certain software tools I  think might help you guys as  entrepreneurs so I'll be afternoon and  then I'll also do another chunk of email  so I still have the three chunks one is  the 10 minutes sorry the ten o'clock  video the afternoon videos and the  emails so again I try to keep everything  the three main chunks of work every day  and then that kind of keeps paying vigor  a Turkey's been going gives me some  breaks in between and every day has its  own day that I new tasks that I have  each day and it kind of keeps me excited  to keep going so once it's a lot of fun  I know after hour you know I have my  email still every day but the rest of  the day is all fun stuff answering  questions like yours and doing other  video tutorials so when's there's a lot  of fun and then on Thursday Thursday  would be my meeting day and then a  little bit more CEO time so thursday  again I'll cut back to the one o'clock  I'll come in i'll do email and then for  the two chunks I'll do meetings and  either more meetings or CEO time again  so I booked all my meetings on thursdays  thursdays after I've done my email and  I'll either do a phone calls will do  kind of schedule them all back to back  or if somebody's coming to meet me we'll  meet at the starbucks in my building i  have a starbucks on the ground floor and  i'll come and have meetings there and  we'll be back to back to back so  everybody gets up to an hour of time  and that's that's what will happen so  we'll meet I'll have a meeting have  another meeting have another meeting or  do phone calls in between so I booked  everything for Thursday it just kind of  gets me in the space of of meeting  people and I find is less mental  shifting so it's easier to get stuff  done where if I had a meeting on Tuesday  and I'm meeting Wednesday a meeting  Thursday then every time I got to think  okay what am I going to do with this  meeting what are we talking about just  getting the minds of getting ready to  meet people instead of working on  projects and I find if I can chunk all  that into one day it makes it a lot  easier for me to kind of get it all done  and do it all at once so depending on  how many meetings or phone calls I have  the second chunk might be CEO time again  to work on projects or could just be  meetings when I finish the day on  Thursday I usually put an autoresponder  on my email saying that I'm away until  Monday afternoon we'll all get back to  them whoever emails me so that's my  typical day my typical week I guess in  the life of my monday the thursday  sometimes I you know I still experiment  with this with this plan I would usually  much rather do mornings than then  afternoons but because of my family  situation my wife teaches salsa so she's  always available in the mornings instead  of at night where she's teaching at  night and my son goes to school in the  afternoon and right now he's available  in the morning so we have mornings  together so we try to keep to that but  in general what I would love to do is  have my mornings will work on big  projects and then check email in the  afternoon the one time will kind of get  an exception to this is if I'm really  working on something to find a lot of  momentum then I want to ke